{"availability":"available","full":"j8asic/SpeciaLUT","name":"SpeciaLUT","description":"Runtime choosing of template specializations using compile-time lookup-tables. Compile all states of a template function, but execute the optimal one at runtime.","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":28,"forks":2,"created":"2021-05-14T09:46:41Z","updated":"2025-12-31T09:08:04Z","license":"BSD-2-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["compile-time","compile-time-meta-programming","cpp","cpp17","cpp20","cuda","header-only","lookup-tables","metaprogramming","modern-cpp","optimization","optimization-algorithms","specialization"],"demo":"https://godbolt.org/z/Gzc87hPG6","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:48.467Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:48.467Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:48.467Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:37:55.377Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:38.992Z","stars":28,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:48.467Z","stars":28,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SpeciaLUT is designed for hot functions with:","The library pre-compiles all possible specializations and selects the right one at runtime via a lookup table. This eliminates branching overhead inside tight loops."],"features":["Many iterations inside the function (loops over large data)","Multiple if/else or enum-based control flow that creates branching","Conditions that are loop-invariant (set once before the function, used many times inside)","GPU kernels (CUDA/HIP) — avoids warp divergence","Large functions that can't be inlined"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/j8asic/SpeciaLUT/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"535cafee5cc8fd69738a990ec3c3840410c031ce47592dad4ef5db973748808b","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T05:59:43.641Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:13:28.394Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-12-31T09:08:04Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SpeciaLUT is designed for hot functio